 mojo/stdlib/std/subprocess/subprocess.mojo           | 2 +-
 6 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

=== Add unsafe_ prefix to Pointer ===
    `unsafe_strided_load`, `unsafe_strided_store`, `unsafe_gather`,
    `unsafe_scatter`, `unsafe_as_noalias`, `unsafe_address_space_cast`,
    `unsafe_take_pointee`) for pointer operations that
    are individually unsafe, rather than requiring the whole pointer to be
    typed
    unsafe. This lets `Pointer` stay a single type while each unsafe
    operation is
    marked explicitly at the call site.
    
    The old unprefixed names remain as thin wrappers for compatibility, but
    are
    now hidden from generated docs and still require an unsafe pointer to
    call.
    
    MODULAR_ORIG_COMMIT_REV_ID: c3412275abd8694c8b0c8d410ac7034b364c5eda

